 >> opentype/STAT/ital_axis
    Ensure VFs have 'ital' STAT axis.
    

    Rationale:                                                                
                                                                               
    Check that related Upright and Italic VFs have an 'ital' axis in the STAT  
    table.                                                                     
                                                                               
    Since the STAT table can be used to create new instances, it is important  
    to ensure that such an 'ital' axis be the last one declared in the STAT    
    table so that the eventual naming of new instances follows the subfamily   
    traditional scheme (RIBBI / WWS) where "Italic" is always last.            
                                                                               
    The 'ital' axis should also be strictly boolean, only accepting values of  
    0 (for Uprights) or 1 (for Italics). This usually works as a mechanism     
    for selecting between two linked variable font files.                      
                                                                               
    Also, the axis value name for uprights must be set as elidable.            
                                                                               
    More info: https://github.com/fonttools/fontbakery/issues/2934
               https://github.com/fonttools/fontbakery/issues/3668
               https://github.com/fonttools/fontbakery/issues/3669

